header, including those peachq contributors have changed since the fork; git
history (git log 654ea443..HEAD -- <file>) shows every such change. Files added
since the fork carry the peachq contributors header.

Major changes since the fork (KX dev at 654ea443):

- Telemetry and KX prompts removed: no Application Insights reporter, no
  survey or newsletter prompts; bug and feature links point at this fork.
- Renamed to timestored.peachq, with peachq.* settings, commands and views.
- Coexists with the KX extension (pauses its q features where KX is enabled)
  and imports the KX extension's connections and settings.
- CI on GitHub Actions; the injected q code is tested with qunit on peachq.
- Per-platform packages bundle peachq and list a built-in peachq connection.
- REPL: quiet start, and an error in a query no longer stalls the REPL.
- Query sending and results: per-connection query modes, a qStudio-style
  wrapper with typed replies, results in the console and the grid together.
- Whole-file command: "Execute Whole File as if loaded with \l".

Third-party components:

- peachq (https://peachq.org), MIT licence. Each per-platform package ships
  the peachq binary with its LICENSE and NOTICE in bin/peachq/<target>/.
- Test scripts under test/fixtures/l-diff/third-party/ are copied unchanged
  from the projects listed in its SOURCES.md, each with its licence (MIT or
  CC0 1.0). They are used by the test suite only and are not shipped in the
  extension package.

